  "provenance": "fuzz-regression",
  "provenance_note": "Fuzz regression for issue #433 (nightly run 42806757101, target tc_decode, artefact crash-e2130b2c92d9ea806638d99ce39eab0008793de8). The crash was in the fuzz target, not the codec: it re-encoded every strict decode that check_frame accepts and assumed that meant a configured MAP, but a frame whose Segment Header names a MAP ID the channels do not hold passes the Frame Validation Checks (232.0-B-4 Cor. 1 \u00a74.4.9.3.3 tests the Transfer Frame Header and the FECF only; TC-022, OI-98). The frame is the 7 octets the fuzzer produced (AD, SCID 0x155, VC 2 with a Segment Header, no FECF, Segment Header FE = flags 11, MAP 62, one data octet FD), read off the octets by the field widths of \u00a74.1.2 and \u00a74.1.3. Expected values are the codec's behaviour as TC-022 states it; no independent model covers this file.",
